# The Vault EC2's API process — SAME codebase and SAME unit shape as
# infra/aws/systemd/rawprod-api.service (identical hardening block, identical ExecStart), running
# on its own instance with its own security group, its own IAM role, and its own env file. Every
# hardening comment in rawprod-api.service applies here unchanged and is not repeated.
#
# ── WHAT "vault-only module set" MEANS TODAY, AND WHY THIS UNIT DOES NOT DO IT ─────────────────
#
# The lane brief asked for "the separate codebase, vault-only module set if the app supports it —
# otherwise document." It does not, and this is that documentation, not a workaround:
#
#   backend/api/src/app.module.ts imports EVERY cluster unconditionally (ClusterOrgModule,
#   ClusterProcurementModule, FormulaModule, ProductionModule, ... all 15+ of them) — there is no
#   env-gated subset, no separate vault-only entrypoint, no build target that drops the
#   non-formula clusters. `main.ts` boots the whole AppModule or it boots nothing.
#
#   backend/backend-kernel/src/config/config.schema.ts's DATABASE_URL is NOT optional
#   (`z.string().url()`, no `.optional()`) — the process refuses to start without a "main" schema
#   connection at all, because JwtAuthGuard / PermissionsGuard / the iam.user_master-backed auth
#   path every request goes through (app.module.ts's global APP_GUARD providers) need the iam and
#   platform schemas to exist on THAT connection, not just formula.
#
# So vault-api.service, as configured, is the FULL application — every route the main EC2 serves
# is also technically reachable here — with FORMULA_DATABASE_URL pointed at the real, isolated
# vault-pg (ra_vault role) and DATABASE_URL pointed, FOR NOW, at the SAME shared `rawprod`
# database the main EC2 uses (read the identity/RBAC tables it needs to boot and authenticate
# requests at all). THIS IS AN INTERIM COMPROMISE, NOT THE PLAN'S TARGET SHAPE:
# MIGRATION_AWS_PLAN.md §2 draws vault-db's security group accepting 5432 from vault-app ONLY,
# with no path back to alembic-pg — true to that diagram, THIS unit's vault-app-SG-scoped
# instance role must currently ALSO reach alembic-pg for DATABASE_URL, which is exactly the
# shared-credential path §109.1 exists to close. What DOES hold today, and is real isolation
# rather than documentation of a gap: the vault-app SG has no public listener (allow-list only,
# infra/aws/nginx/vault-allowlist.conf), FORMULA_DATABASE_URL is a distinct role on a distinct
# RDS instance with its own CMK, and rawprod_app (the main EC2's DML role) has no grant on
# vault-pg at all — the DATA is isolated even though the PROCESS is not yet.
#
# Closing this gap needs one of: (a) a real vault-only NestJS entrypoint (a second main.ts
# importing only FormulaModule + the minimal auth surface it needs — app code, not ops, tracked
# under PB-03), or (b) a read-scoped iam/platform replica reachable from vault-app's SG instead of
# a live connection to alembic-pg. Neither is built here; this unit and this comment are the
# honest current state, not a claim that §109's separate-trust-domain requirement is met.

[Unit]
Description=Vault API (RawProd codebase, restricted network exposure — see comment above)
After=network-online.target vault-migrate.service
Requires=vault-migrate.service

[Service]
Type=exec
User=rawprod
Group=rawprod
WorkingDirectory=/srv/rawprod/app
EnvironmentFile=/etc/rawprod/vault.env
ExecStart=/opt/node-v22.12.0/bin/node --import @swc-node/register/esm-register backend/api/src/main.ts

# G6: logs to a file the CloudWatch agent ships to /rawaroma/rawprod/vault-api (PID1 opens it, so ProtectSystem=strict is fine)
StandardOutput=append:/var/log/rawprod/vault-api.log
StandardError=append:/var/log/rawprod/vault-api.log
KillSignal=SIGTERM
TimeoutStopSec=30
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5s

NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
PrivateDevices=true
RestrictAddressFamilies=AF_INET AF_INET6 AF_UNIX
LockPersonality=true

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
